## 1. Definitions

### 1.1 “Software”

“Software” means PickleAI, including its source code, scripts, documentation, configuration files, assets, and other materials distributed by Carter Sparks as part of the PickleAI project.

### 1.2 “Original Developer”

“Original Developer” means **Carter Sparks**.

### 1.3 “Official Project”

“Official Project” means the PickleAI project maintained at:

https://github.com/PickleForge-Labs/PickleAI

### 1.4 “Modification”

“Modification” means any alteration, addition, deletion, extension, adaptation, fork, or derivative work based on or incorporating the Software.

### 1.5 “Non-Commercial Use”

“Non-Commercial Use” means use that is not primarily intended to generate revenue, commercial advantage, or monetary compensation.

Examples may include:

* Personal projects
* Hobby projects
* Educational projects
* School projects
* Research projects
* Demonstrations
* Non-profit community projects
* Personal experimentation
* Free software projects that do not commercially exploit PickleAI

### 1.6 “Commercial Use”

“Commercial Use” means use primarily intended to generate revenue, commercial advantage, or monetary compensation.

Commercial Use includes, without limitation:

* Selling the Software
* Selling a Modification
* Including the Software in a paid product
* Including the Software in a paid service
* Offering PickleAI as a paid hosted service
* Using PickleAI as part of a commercial business operation
* Commercial redistribution
* OEM distribution
* Proprietary enterprise deployment
* Commercial SaaS use
* Licensing PickleAI or a Modification to another party for payment

